I find most of my deaths are due to my own negligence or diving too
fast or something else that is player controllable.  For comparison,
on my own PC where I'm just goofing around speed playing, I probably
have an ascension rate of 5% But when I actually focus, and tell
myself I WILL ascend this game, most of the time I do unless something
absolutely tragic happens.  I have had one of those nasty deaths by
trickery in the Plane of Water, and those hurt even more than deaths
induced by your own stupidity. :(

What helps me is to analyze what went wrong with each death, and note
to myself how to prevent it in the future.  Don't get too discouraged,
think of it as a learning experience.  My personal playing style, I
get the most enjoyment when I play at a medium speed.  Many death
situations can be avoidable but playing ultra ultra safe is a bit
boring to me. *shrug*

